{"id": "medication-metformin-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "medication", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Metformin instructions (made-up example)", "original": "Medication Instructions: Metformin 500 mg. Take 1 tablet by mouth twice daily with breakfast and dinner. Metformin helps lower blood sugar in type 2 diabetes. Taking it with food helps prevent an upset stomach. Your tablets are extended-release: do not crush or chew them. Check your blood sugar as your care team instructed. Before any test that uses contrast dye, stop taking metformin and call your doctor. Questions? Call Riverbend Pharmacy at (919) 555-0102.", "target": {"title": "Your medicine: metformin", "language": "en", "source": "Metformin instructions (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Your medicine", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Your medicine is **metformin 500 mg**.", "picture": "pill"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It **lowers** your **blood sugar**.", "picture": "blood sugar"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It is for **type 2 diabetes**.", "picture": "diabetes"}]}, {"topic": "How to take it", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Take **1 tablet**.", "picture": "pill"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Twice** a day.", "picture": "calendar"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "With **breakfast** and **dinner**.", "picture": "meal"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Swallow it **by mouth**.", "picture": "mouth"}]}, {"topic": "Food helps", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Take it with **food**.", "picture": "meal"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "This helps your **stomach**.", "picture": "stomach"}]}, {"topic": "Swallow it whole", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Do **not crush** the tablet.", "picture": "crush pill"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Do **not chew** it.", "picture": "no chewing"}]}, {"topic": "Check your blood sugar", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Check your **blood sugar**.", "picture": "blood sugar test"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Do it the way your **care team** said.", "picture": "doctor"}]}, {"topic": "Before some tests", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "A test with **contrast dye**?", "picture": "x-ray"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Stop** metformin first.", "picture": "stop"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Call** your **doctor**.", "picture": "doctor"}]}, {"topic": "Questions?", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Call **Riverbend Pharmacy**.", "picture": "pharmacy"}, {"kind": "phone", "text": "Pharmacy: (919) 555-0102", "picture": "phone"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": ["'Extended-release' is not named on the handout; the page just says swallow it whole. Please confirm."]}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "medication-schedule-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "medication", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Daily medication schedule form (made-up example)", "original": "Daily Medication Schedule for: ____________. Updated on: ____________. Morning: medication ____________ dose ____________. Midday: medication ____________ dose ____________. Evening: medication ____________ dose ____________. Bedtime: medication ____________ dose ____________. [ ] Take with food [ ] Take with a full glass of water [ ] Do not drive after taking. Bring this schedule and all your pill bottles to every appointment. Pharmacy phone: ____________.", "target": {"title": "My medicine schedule", "language": "en", "source": "Daily medication schedule form (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "My medicine schedule", "lines": [{"kind": "blank", "text": "For: ____________", "picture": "person"}, {"kind": "blank", "text": "Updated on: ____________", "picture": "calendar"}]}, {"topic": "Morning", "lines": [{"kind": "blank", "text": "Medicine: ____________", "picture": "sunrise"}, {"kind": "blank", "text": "Dose: ____________", "picture": "pill"}]}, {"topic": "Midday", "lines": [{"kind": "blank", "text": "Medicine: ____________", "picture": "sun"}, {"kind": "blank", "text": "Dose: ____________", "picture": "pill"}]}, {"topic": "Evening", "lines": [{"kind": "blank", "text": "Medicine: ____________", "picture": "sunset"}, {"kind": "blank", "text": "Dose: ____________", "picture": "pill"}]}, {"topic": "Bedtime", "lines": [{"kind": "blank", "text": "Medicine: ____________", "picture": "bed"}, {"kind": "blank", "text": "Dose: ____________", "picture": "pill"}]}, {"topic": "Remember", "lines": [{"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Take with **food**.", "picture": "meal"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Take with a full glass of **water**.", "picture": "glass of water"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Do **not drive** after taking.", "picture": "no driving"}]}, {"topic": "Bring to every visit", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Bring this **schedule**.", "picture": "schedule"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Bring all your **pill bottles**.", "picture": "pill bottle"}, {"kind": "blank", "text": "Pharmacy phone: ____________", "picture": "phone"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": ["Fill-in form: the clinician or pharmacist writes the medicines and ticks the reminders."]}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "appointment-neuro-en-003", "language": "en", "doc_type": "appointment", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Neurology appointment reminder (made-up example)", "original": "Appointment Reminder. You have a follow-up appointment with Dr. Hannah Brooks, Neurology, on Friday, April 9, 2027 at 2:45 p.m. Location: Westfield Medical Plaza, 600 Oakmont Drive, Suite 310. Park in the garage on Level 2 and bring your parking ticket to the front desk. Please bring your blood pressure log and a list of your current medications. If you need to cancel, please call at least 24 hours in advance: (919) 555-0103.", "target": {"title": "Your appointment", "language": "en", "source": "Neurology appointment reminder (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Your appointment", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "See **Dr. Hannah Brooks**.", "picture": "doctor"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "She is in **Neurology**.", "picture": "brain"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Friday, April 9, 2027**", "picture": "calendar"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**2:45 p.m.**", "picture": "clock"}]}, {"topic": "Where", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "**Westfield Medical Plaza**", "picture": "hospital"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**600 Oakmont Drive, Suite 310**", "picture": "map"}]}, {"topic": "Parking", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Park in the **garage**.", "picture": "parking garage"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Go to **Level 2**.", "picture": "level"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Bring your **parking ticket** to the **front desk**.", "picture": "ticket"}]}, {"topic": "What to bring", "lines": [{"kind": "step", "text": "Your **blood pressure** log.", "picture": "blood pressure"}, {"kind": "step", "text": "A **list** of your **medicines**.", "picture": "medicine list"}]}, {"topic": "Need to cancel?", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Call at least **24 hours** before.", "picture": "clock"}, {"kind": "phone", "text": "Phone: (919) 555-0103", "picture": "phone"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": ["'She' assumes the doctor's pronoun; edit if needed."]}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "appointment-missed-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "appointment", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Missed appointment letter (made-up example)", "original": "We Missed You. Our records show that you missed your speech therapy appointment on Monday, March 22, 2027. Regular attendance is important for your progress. Please call Piedmont Speech Clinic at (919) 555-0104 within 2 weeks to reschedule. If we do not hear from you, your referral may be closed and you may need a new referral from your doctor. If transportation is a problem, ask about our free ride program.", "target": {"title": "We missed you", "language": "en", "source": "Missed appointment letter (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "You missed a visit", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "You **missed** your **speech therapy** visit.", "picture": "speech therapist"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Monday, March 22, 2027**", "picture": "calendar"}]}, {"topic": "Coming helps", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Coming **every time** helps you **improve**.", "picture": "improve"}]}, {"topic": "If you do not call", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Your **referral** may be **closed**.", "picture": "closed"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "You may need a **new referral** from your **doctor**.", "picture": "doctor"}]}, {"topic": "Need a ride?", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Ask about our **free ride** program.", "picture": "car"}]}, {"topic": "Call us", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "**Call** to make a **new visit**.", "picture": "phone"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Call within **2 weeks**.", "picture": "calendar"}, {"kind": "phone", "text": "Piedmont Speech Clinic: (919) 555-0104", "picture": "phone"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": []}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "consent-recording-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "consent", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Consent for audio and video recording (made-up example)", "original": "Consent for Audio and Video Recording. During speech therapy, your therapist may record your sessions. Recordings help track your progress and may be used for training students. Recordings are stored securely and are not shared outside Piedmont Speech Clinic without your written permission. You may say no. Saying no will not affect your care. You may change your mind at any time by telling your therapist. Please choose: [ ] I agree to recording for tracking my progress. [ ] I agree to recording for training students. [ ] I do not agree to recording. Signature: ____________ Date: ____________", "target": {"title": "Recording your therapy", "language": "en", "source": "Consent for audio and video recording (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Recording your therapy", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Your therapist may **record** your sessions.", "picture": "video camera"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Sound** and **video**.", "picture": "microphone"}]}, {"topic": "Why record?", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "To see your **progress**.", "picture": "chart"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "To **teach** students.", "picture": "students"}]}, {"topic": "Your recordings are safe", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "They are kept **safe**.", "picture": "lock"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "They stay at **Piedmont Speech Clinic**.", "picture": "clinic"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Shared outside **only** if you say **yes** in writing.", "picture": "signature"}]}, {"topic": "You choose", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "You can say **no**.", "picture": "no"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Saying no does **not change** your **care**.", "picture": "care"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "You can **change your mind** any time.", "picture": "change"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Just tell your **therapist**.", "picture": "speech therapist"}]}, {"topic": "Please choose", "lines": [{"kind": "checkbox", "text": "**Yes**, record me to see my **progress**.", "picture": "yes"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "**Yes**, record me to **teach** students.", "picture": "yes"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "**No**, do not record me.", "picture": "no"}]}, {"topic": "Sign", "lines": [{"kind": "blank", "text": "Signature: ____________", "picture": "signature"}, {"kind": "blank", "text": "Date: ____________", "picture": "calendar"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": ["Consent form: the clinic's privacy or legal team should also approve the wording before use."]}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "insurance-approval-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "insurance", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Insurance authorization notice (made-up example)", "original": "Notice of Authorization. Member: Robert Hayes. Member ID: XJH448213. Your health plan, Carolina Community Health Plan, has approved 12 outpatient speech therapy visits at Piedmont Speech Clinic. These visits must be used between January 4, 2027 and June 30, 2027. Your copay is $20 per visit. If you need more visits, your therapist must send a new request before your approved visits run out. If you have questions about your benefits, call Member Services at 1-800-555-0105, TTY 711.", "target": {"title": "Your therapy is approved", "language": "en", "source": "Insurance authorization notice (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Your therapy is approved", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "For: **Robert Hayes**", "picture": "person"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Member ID: **XJH448213**", "picture": "card"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Your **health plan** said **yes**.", "picture": "yes"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Carolina Community Health Plan**", "picture": "insurance card"}]}, {"topic": "How many visits", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "**12 speech therapy** visits.", "picture": "speech therapist"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "At **Piedmont Speech Clinic**.", "picture": "clinic"}]}, {"topic": "When", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Use them between **January 4, 2027**", "picture": "calendar"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "and **June 30, 2027**.", "picture": "calendar"}]}, {"topic": "Cost", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "You pay **$20** each visit.", "picture": "money"}]}, {"topic": "Need more visits?", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Your **therapist** must **ask** for more.", "picture": "speech therapist"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Before your visits **run out**.", "picture": "calendar"}]}, {"topic": "Questions?", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Call **Member Services**.", "picture": "help"}, {"kind": "phone", "text": "Phone: 1-800-555-0105", "picture": "phone"}, {"kind": "phone", "text": "TTY: 711", "picture": "tty"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": []}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "home-program-words-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "home_program", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Home program: word finding (made-up example)", "original": "Home Program: Word Retrieval Practice. Complete the checked activities for 15 minutes, 5 days per week. [ ] Name 10 items in a category (e.g., foods, animals, clothing). [ ] Describe a photo out loud using 3 sentences. [ ] Practice your personal script daily. [ ] Read a short news story aloud and summarize it in 1 sentence. [ ] Use the naming app recommended by your therapist. [ ] Write a grocery list without help. Record your practice on the log sheet and bring it to your next session. Your therapist: ____________", "target": {"title": "Practice finding words", "language": "en", "source": "Home program: word finding (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Practice at home", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Practice finding **words** at home.", "picture": "practice"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**15 minutes** a day.", "picture": "clock"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**5 days** a week.", "picture": "calendar"}]}, {"topic": "Do the checked activities", "lines": [{"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Name **10 things** in a group (foods, animals, clothes).", "picture": "food"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Describe a **photo** out loud in **3 sentences**.", "picture": "photo"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Practice your **script** every day.", "picture": "script"}]}, {"topic": "More activities", "lines": [{"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Read a short **news story** out loud. Tell it in **1 sentence**.", "picture": "newspaper"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Use the **naming app** your therapist chose.", "picture": "phone app"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Write a **grocery list** without help.", "picture": "grocery list"}]}, {"topic": "Keep track", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Write your practice on the **log sheet**.", "picture": "log sheet"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Bring** it to your next **session**.", "picture": "speech therapist"}, {"kind": "blank", "text": "Your therapist: ____________", "picture": "speech therapist"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": []}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "results-cognitive-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "results", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Cognitive-communication evaluation summary (made-up example)", "original": "Cognitive-Communication Evaluation: Summary for ____________. Areas assessed: attention, memory, problem solving, and executive function (planning and organization). Findings: [ ] Reduced sustained attention [ ] Reduced short-term memory [ ] Difficulty with problem solving [ ] Difficulty with planning and organization [ ] Within normal limits. Recommendations: [ ] Use a calendar or planner daily [ ] Set phone alarms for medications [ ] Reduce distractions during conversations [ ] Supervision for managing finances [ ] Supervision for driving decisions; discuss with physician. Follow-up: cognitive-communication therapy ___ sessions per week.", "target": {"title": "Your thinking skills results", "language": "en", "source": "Cognitive-communication evaluation summary (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Your results", "lines": [{"kind": "blank", "text": "Results for: ____________", "picture": "person"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "We tested your **attention**, **memory** and **problem solving**.", "picture": "brain"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "And how you **plan** and **organize**.", "picture": "plan"}]}, {"topic": "What we found", "lines": [{"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Hard to **pay attention** for a long time.", "picture": "attention"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Hard to **remember** new things.", "picture": "memory"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Hard to **solve problems**.", "picture": "puzzle"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Hard to **plan** and **organize**.", "picture": "plan"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Your results are **normal**.", "picture": "check mark"}]}, {"topic": "Tips that help", "lines": [{"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Use a **calendar** or **planner** every day.", "picture": "calendar"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Set **phone alarms** for your **medicines**.", "picture": "alarm"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "Turn off **noise** when you **talk**.", "picture": "quiet"}]}, {"topic": "Get help with", "lines": [{"kind": "checkbox", "text": "**Money** and **bills**: get help.", "picture": "money"}, {"kind": "checkbox", "text": "**Driving**: get help to decide. Talk to your **doctor**.", "picture": "car"}]}, {"topic": "Your therapy", "lines": [{"kind": "blank", "text": "Therapy: ___ times a week.", "picture": "calendar"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": ["'Reduce distractions during conversations' became 'Turn off noise when you talk'; please check this covers it.", "'Supervision' became 'get help'. Please confirm this is strong enough."]}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "discharge-therapy-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "discharge", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Speech therapy discharge summary (made-up example)", "original": "Discharge Summary: Outpatient Speech Therapy. Patient: Linda Marsh. Dates of service: September 8, 2026 to January 29, 2027. Total sessions: 32. Goals met: improved word finding in conversation; independent use of a communication notebook. Goal partially met: reading paragraphs. Recommendations: continue the home program 4 days per week; attend the Aphasia Café community group. Return to therapy if you notice new changes in your speech or language. To restart therapy, ask your doctor for a new referral or call (919) 555-0106.", "target": {"title": "Your speech therapy is finished", "language": "en", "source": "Speech therapy discharge summary (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Therapy is finished", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "For: **Linda Marsh**", "picture": "person"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Your **speech therapy** is **finished**.", "picture": "finish"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "From **September 8, 2026** to **January 29, 2027**.", "picture": "calendar"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "You came **32 times**.", "picture": "calendar"}]}, {"topic": "What you can do now", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "You **find words** better when you **talk**.", "picture": "conversation"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "You use your **communication notebook** on your own.", "picture": "notebook"}]}, {"topic": "Still working on", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "You are still working on **reading paragraphs**.", "picture": "read"}]}, {"topic": "Keep going", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Do your **home practice** **4 days** a week.", "picture": "practice"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Go to the **Aphasia Café** group.", "picture": "coffee"}]}, {"topic": "Come back if", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "New **changes** in your **speech** or **language**?", "picture": "speech"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Ask your **doctor** for a **new referral**.", "picture": "doctor"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Or **call** us.", "picture": "phone"}, {"kind": "phone", "text": "Phone: (919) 555-0106", "picture": "phone"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": []}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "education-aphasia-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "education", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Aphasia information for patients and families (made-up example)", "original": "Aphasia: Information for Patients and Families. Aphasia is an acquired language disorder caused by damage to the language areas of the brain, most often from a stroke. It can affect speaking, understanding, reading, and writing. Aphasia does not affect intelligence. People with aphasia know what they want to say but may have trouble finding the words. Speech-language therapy can improve communication, and many people continue to improve for years. Communication partners can help by speaking slowly, using short sentences, writing key words, and allowing extra time. For more information, contact Piedmont Speech Clinic at (919) 555-0107.", "target": {"title": "What is aphasia?", "language": "en", "source": "Aphasia information for patients and families (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "What is aphasia?", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Aphasia is a **language** problem.", "picture": "speech bubble"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It comes from **damage** to the **brain**.", "picture": "brain"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Most often from a **stroke**.", "picture": "stroke"}]}, {"topic": "What it affects", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "**Speaking**", "picture": "talk"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Understanding**", "picture": "listen"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Reading**", "picture": "read"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Writing**", "picture": "write"}]}, {"topic": "You are still smart", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Aphasia does **not** change how **smart** you are.", "picture": "brain"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "You **know** what you want to say.", "picture": "idea"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Finding the **words** can be **hard**.", "picture": "search"}]}, {"topic": "It can get better", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "**Speech therapy** can help.", "picture": "speech therapist"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Many people **improve** for **years**.", "picture": "improve"}]}, {"topic": "How others can help", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Speak **slowly**.", "picture": "slow"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Use **short** sentences.", "picture": "short"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Write** key words.", "picture": "write"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Give **extra time**.", "picture": "clock"}]}, {"topic": "More information", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Call **Piedmont Speech Clinic**.", "picture": "clinic"}, {"kind": "phone", "text": "Phone: (919) 555-0107", "picture": "phone"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": []}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "mental-health-anxiety-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "mental_health", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Managing anxiety after a stroke (made-up example)", "original": "Managing Anxiety After a Stroke. Anxiety, such as feeling worried, nervous, or panicky, is common after a stroke. Strategies that may help: slow breathing (breathe in for 4 counts, out for 6 counts), regular physical activity as approved by your doctor, keeping a daily routine, and talking with people you trust. Tell your doctor if anxiety makes it hard to sleep, eat, or do daily activities. Counseling is available through Oak Valley Counseling Center; call (919) 555-0108. If you are in crisis or thinking about suicide, call or text 988, the 988 Suicide & Crisis Lifeline.", "target": {"title": "Feeling anxious after a stroke", "language": "en", "source": "Managing anxiety after a stroke (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Feeling anxious", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Many people feel **worried** after a **stroke**.", "picture": "worried"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Or **nervous**, or **panicky**.", "picture": "nervous"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "This is **common**.", "picture": "group of people"}]}, {"topic": "Slow breathing", "lines": [{"kind": "step", "text": "Breathe **in**. Count to **4**.", "picture": "breathe in"}, {"kind": "step", "text": "Breathe **out**. Count to **6**.", "picture": "breathe out"}]}, {"topic": "Other things that help", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "**Move** your body, if your **doctor** says okay.", "picture": "walk"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Keep a **daily routine**.", "picture": "calendar"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Talk** with people you **trust**.", "picture": "conversation"}]}, {"topic": "Tell your doctor", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Hard to **sleep**, **eat** or do **daily things**?", "picture": "bed"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Tell** your **doctor**.", "picture": "doctor"}]}, {"topic": "Counseling", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "You can talk to a **counselor**.", "picture": "counselor"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Oak Valley Counseling Center**", "picture": "building"}, {"kind": "phone", "text": "Phone: (919) 555-0108", "picture": "phone"}]}, {"topic": "Help now", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "In **crisis**? Thinking about **suicide**?", "picture": "help"}, {"kind": "crisis", "text": "Call or text 988 — 988 Suicide & Crisis Lifeline", "picture": "phone"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": []}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "procedure-ultrasound-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "procedure", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Carotid ultrasound instructions (made-up example)", "original": "Carotid Ultrasound: What to Expect. Your doctor ordered a carotid ultrasound to check blood flow in the arteries in your neck. The test is painless and uses sound waves, not radiation. It takes about 30 minutes. Wear a shirt with a loose collar and do not wear necklaces. You will lie on your back while a technician moves a small wand with gel over your neck. You can eat, drink, and take your medicines as usual. Your appointment: Thursday, March 11, 2027 at 8:15 a.m., Northgate Imaging Center, 4410 Pinecrest Parkway. Questions: (919) 555-0111.", "target": {"title": "Your neck ultrasound", "language": "en", "source": "Carotid ultrasound instructions (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Your neck ultrasound", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Your doctor wants a **neck ultrasound**.", "picture": "ultrasound"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It checks **blood flow** in your **neck**.", "picture": "neck"}]}, {"topic": "It does not hurt", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "The test does **not hurt**.", "picture": "no pain"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It uses **sound waves**.", "picture": "sound waves"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**No radiation**.", "picture": "no radiation"}]}, {"topic": "When and where", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "**Thursday, March 11, 2027**", "picture": "calendar"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**8:15 a.m.**", "picture": "clock"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Northgate Imaging Center**", "picture": "hospital"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**4410 Pinecrest Parkway**", "picture": "map"}]}, {"topic": "What to wear", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Wear a shirt with a **loose collar**.", "picture": "shirt"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**No necklaces**.", "picture": "no necklace"}]}, {"topic": "During the test", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "You **lie on your back**.", "picture": "lie down"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "A small **wand** with **gel** moves over your neck.", "picture": "ultrasound"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "It takes about **30 minutes**.", "picture": "clock"}]}, {"topic": "Food and medicine", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "You can **eat** and **drink**.", "picture": "eat"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Take your **medicines** as usual.", "picture": "pill"}]}, {"topic": "Questions?", "lines": [{"kind": "phone", "text": "Questions? Call (919) 555-0111", "picture": "phone"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": ["'Carotid' is not used on the handout; it says 'neck ultrasound'. Please confirm."]}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
{"id": "education-falls-en-001", "language": "en", "doc_type": "education", "split": "train", "provenance": "made-up (written for this project)", "license": "CC BY 4.0 (project-authored)", "slp_reviewed": true, "source": "Preventing falls at home after a stroke (made-up example)", "original": "Preventing Falls at Home After a Stroke. Weakness, balance problems, and changes in vision can increase your risk of falling. To reduce your risk: remove throw rugs; keep walkways clear of cords and clutter; use night-lights in the bedroom, hallway, and bathroom; install grab bars near the toilet and in the shower; and wear shoes with non-slip soles. Use your cane or walker as your physical therapist taught you. If you fall and are hurt, or cannot get up, call 911.", "target": {"title": "Stop falls at home", "language": "en", "source": "Preventing falls at home after a stroke (made-up example)", "pages": [{"topic": "Stop falls at home", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "After a stroke, falls are **more likely**.", "picture": "fall"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "**Weakness**, **balance** problems and **vision** changes can cause falls.", "picture": "balance"}]}, {"topic": "Clear the floor", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "**Remove** throw rugs.", "picture": "rug"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Keep walkways **clear**.", "picture": "hallway"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "No **cords** or **clutter** on the floor.", "picture": "cord"}]}, {"topic": "Light and grab bars", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Use **night-lights**: bedroom, hallway, bathroom.", "picture": "night-light"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Put **grab bars** by the **toilet**.", "picture": "grab bar"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "And in the **shower**.", "picture": "shower"}]}, {"topic": "Walk safely", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Wear shoes with **non-slip** soles.", "picture": "shoes"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Use your **cane** or **walker**.", "picture": "walker"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Use it the way your **therapist** taught you.", "picture": "physical therapist"}]}, {"topic": "If you fall", "lines": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Are you **hurt**?", "picture": "pain"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "You **cannot get up**?", "picture": "fall"}, {"kind": "crisis", "text": "Call 911", "picture": "ambulance"}]}], "notes_for_reviewer": ["'Install grab bars' became 'Put grab bars'."]}, "reviewed_by": "CCC-SLP (anonymous)", "review_date": "2026-11-11"}
